== Configuration Options ==

=== SliderData Format ===

The '''SliderData''' element contains the slider configuration in a pipe-separated format. It can be specified either as text content or as a class attribute.

'''Format:''' <code>SlideCount|Interval|Height|Orientation|Width|CaptionPosition</code>

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Description
! Values
! Example
|-
| SlideCount
| Number of slides in the slider
| Integer
| <code>3</code>
|-
| Interval
| Time between automatic slide changes (in milliseconds)
| Integer (≥1000)
| <code>5000</code>
|-
| Height
| Height of the slider
| <code>auto</code>, pixel value
| <code>auto</code>, <code>300</code>, <code>300px</code>
|-
| Orientation
| Direction of slider movement
| <code>right</code> (horizontal), <code>down</code> (vertical)
| <code>right</code>
|-
| Width
| Width of the slider
| Percentage or pixel value
| <code>100%</code>, <code>500px</code>
|-
| CaptionPosition
| Position of captions (optional)
| <code>top</code>, <code>bottom</code>, <code>overlay</code>
| <code>bottom</code>
|}

You can specify fewer parameters if you don't need all of them:

* '''3 parameters:''' <code>SlideCount|Interval|Height</code>
* '''4 parameters:''' <code>SlideCount|Interval|Height|Orientation</code>
* '''5 parameters:''' <code>SlideCount|Interval|Height|Orientation|Width</code>
* '''6 parameters:''' <code>SlideCount|Interval|Height|Orientation|Width|CaptionPosition</code>

== Slide Options ==

=== Adding Captions ===

To add a caption to a slide, use the <code>data-desc</code> attribute:

<pre>
<div class="Sld" data-desc="This is a caption for the first slide">
  [[File:image1.png]]
</div>
</pre>

=== Making Slides Clickable ===

You can make slides clickable by adding one or more of the following data attributes:

{| class="wikitable"
! Attribute
! Description
! Example
|-
| <code>data-slider-link</code>
| Page name to link to
| <code>Article_Name</code>
|-
| <code>data-slider-link-fandom-wiki</code>
| Fandom wiki to link to
| <code>community</code>
|-
| <code>data-slider-link-external</code>
| External URL
| <code>example.com/page</code>
|}

'''Examples:'''

For a link to a page on the current wiki:
<pre>
<div class="Sld" data-slider-link="Article_Name">
  [[File:image1.png]]
</div>
</pre>

For a link to a page on a specific Fandom wiki:
<pre>
<div class="Sld" data-slider-link="Article_Name" data-slider-link-fandom-wiki="community">
  [[File:image1.png]]
</div>
</pre>

For a link to an external website:
<pre>
<div class="Sld" data-slider-link-external="example.com/page">
  [[File:image1.png]]
</div>
</pre>

== Navigation Button Positioning ==

You can position the navigation buttons using CSS classes on the <code>NavBtns</code> element:

{| class="wikitable"
! Class
! Description
! Example
|-
| <code>nmLeft</code>
| Position buttons on the left side
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmLeft"&gt;</code>
|-
| <code>nmRight</code>
| Position buttons on the right side
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmRight"&gt;</code>
|-
| <code>nmTop</code>
| Position buttons on the top
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmTop"&gt;</code>
|-
| <code>nmBottom</code>
| Position buttons on the bottom
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmBottom"&gt;</code>
|}

=== Navigation Button Alignment ===

You can also align the navigation buttons within their container:

{| class="wikitable"
! Class
! Description
! Example
|-
| <code>nmP1</code>
| Default alignment (start)
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmLeft nmP1"&gt;</code>
|-
| <code>nmP2</code>
| Center alignment
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmLeft nmP2"&gt;</code>
|-
| <code>nmP3</code>
| End alignment
| <code>&lt;div id="NavBtns" class="nmLeft nmP3"&gt;</code>
|}

